From 4b9439fd6826bf22fc4072839a076acdb6016dd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 11:01:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] harden: Tier-3 defense-in-depth backlog (infosvr, libovpn,
 libcodb, rstats, lanauth)

Lower-severity hardening from the 2nd-wave audit; all in-build, all verified by
a full `make rt-be96u` rebuild (gcc-10.3) with zero new warnings at edit sites.

- infosvr/common.c: GETINFO response builders strcpy/sprintf -> strlcpy/snprintf
  (SSID/NetMask/ProductID/FirmwareVersion/PrinterInfo) using sizeof(field).
- libcodb/codb_utils.c: get_backup_db_path_by_datetime built the path with
  source-length strncpy/strncat + sprintf(file_name[40]) into a MAX_FILE_PATH
  (125) buffer -> latent overflow; rebuilt with sized snprintf. (Note: ~6 sibling
  path builders in this file share the same pattern; left as follow-up.)
- libovpn/openvpn_config.c + amvpn_routing.c: custom-config + VPN-director rule
  files written group-rw (0660) -> 0600 (owner only).
- libovpn/openvpn_options.c: fix format/arg mismatch in the residual-parse-state
  logmessage; sanitize the connecting client's username/addresses before they are
  written to client_status (strips control/markup/delimiter chars -> no stored
  corruption/markup feed to the UI).
- libovpn/openvpn_setup.c: unlink the predictable /tmp/ovpn_client_key_%d before
  openvpn writes the tls-crypt-v2 secret (drop pre-planted symlink/file).
- rstats/rstats.c: get/set_meter_file used sizeof(pointer) as the I/O length
  (under-read/write to 4 bytes) -> use the real 64-byte size.
- lanauth/lanauth.c: zero the challenge buffer before each server read so a short
  reply can't leave stale bytes that auth1()/auth2() then hash.

Local branch be96u-only only; never pushed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
